{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The Environment", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "A Pet Whale", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe ways of solving problems and getting things done in social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge  when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "PlaceholderIntegrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge   when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": ". Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention  on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations,   spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to   hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on  a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations,   spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to   hear.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on  a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations,   spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to   hear.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on  a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations,   spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to   hear.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on  a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations,   spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to   hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on   a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations,   spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to   hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Passive: The Present Continuous and Present Perfect Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p>You use the Present Continuous to talk about an action that is happening at the time of speaking. The action or event is in progress. <br/><span class=\"italic\">Environmental groups <span class=\"strong\">are collecting</span> donations through \"adopt-a-whale\" projects. </span></p><p>You use the Present Perfect to talk about a finished action or event with present consequences. There is a connection between what happened in the past and the present.<br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Have</span> you <span class=\"strong\">heard</span> of the movie Free Willy? </span></p>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You often choose the passive form when you want to talk about an action but are not so interested in saying who or what does/did it. Passives without <span class=\"italic\">agents</span> (the doers) are common in academic and scientific writing. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the chart below for the structure of the passive voice.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Name\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">am</span>/<span class=\\\"italic\\\">are</span>/<span class=\\\"italic\\\">is</span> +  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">being </span>+ past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">The money they raise from these \\\"adoptions\\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">is being used</span> to rescue whales from fishing nets.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">have</span>/<span class=\\\"italic\\\">has</span> + <span class=\\\"italic\\\">been </span>+ past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Fortunately, this practice <span class=\\\"strong\\\">has been outlawed</span> since the 1980s. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Humans have always had a fascination with whales. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They have been the subjects of movies and children's stories. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Certain species of whale, like the bowhead whale, have been hunted for their whale oil. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Environmental groups are collecting donations through \"adopt-a-whale\" projects. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The money they raise from these \"adoptions\" is being used to rescue whales from fishing nets, help enforce wildlife protection laws, and do research.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The project is also educating people and public awareness is being raised.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Conditional Sentences", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "There are four types of conditional sentences in English:<ol><li>Zero Conditional - to talk about certainty and facts</li><li>First Conditional - to talk about real possibilities in the present or the future</li><li>Second Conditional - to talk about <span class=\"italic\">unreal</span> possibilities in the present or the future</li><li>Third Conditional - to talk about unreal <span class=\"italic\">past</span> situations</li></ol>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the third conditional to talk about unreal situations in the past. These are things that did not happen in the past. You often use the third conditional to talk about regrets.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the chart below to compare the structure of each kind of conditional:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Conditional Name</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Structure</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Example</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Zero \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span> + Simple Present, Simple Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If you <span class=\\\"strong\\\">heat</span> ice, it <span class=\\\"strong\\\">melts</span>.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"First\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span> + Simple Present, <span class=\\\"italic\\\">will</span> + Simple Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If people <span class=\\\"strong\\\">are made</span> more aware of this issue, further research and development of preservation strategies <span class=\\\"strong\\\">can be achieved</span>.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Second\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span> + Simple Past, <span class=\\\"italic\\\">would</span> + Simple Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If you <span class=\\\"strong\\\">could adopt</span> a whale, <span class=\\\"strong\\\">would</span> you?</span> <br> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">If you<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> were </span>to donate to a charity, which one <span class=\\\"strong\\\">would</span> you choose and why?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Third\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span> + Past Perfect, <span class=\\\"italic\\\">would have</span> + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If this legislation <span class=\\\"strong\\\">had been introduced</span> earlier, the bowhead whale <span class=\\\"strong\\\">would not have become</span> endangered.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Note: In the second conditional, it is grammatically correct to use <span class=\"italic\">If I were ... </span> rather than<span class=\"italic\"> If I was ... </span><br> You may hear people say <span class=\"italic\">If I was ... </span>  in conversation. In writing, you should use <span class=\"italic\">If I were ... </span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "fascination", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having a great interest in something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Humans have always had a fascination with whales.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about endangered species.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "subject", "type": "name"}, {"content": "topic of interest", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Whales have been the subjects of movies and children's  stories.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to gross", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to earn as a total profit", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: 'Free Willy', the movie, grossed 157 million dollars  worldwide.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to be in jeopardy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be in danger", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Today certain whales are in jeopardy of becoming extinct.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to outlaw", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to declare illegal", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Hunting of the bowhead whale was outlawed in the 1980s.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "blubber", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the fat of whales", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Whale oil was obtained by boiling strips of blubber taken   from whales.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "carcass", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the body of a dead animal", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This means killing the whale and oftentimes, disposing of  its carcass.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob10aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to harvest", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to gather", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Blubber was harvested from whales to produce whale oil.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob10aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Watch the movie <span class=\"italic\">Free Willy</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Then, research what happened to the whale that starred in the movie.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss what you found out about the whale. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I watch the movie <span class=\"italic\">Free Willy</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I think about the future of whales in the world.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I identify what happened to the whale from <span class=\"italic\">Free Willy</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I discuss the issue of endangered species.", "type": "text"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob10re1img01.jpg ", "type": "background_image"}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can describe environmental problems.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about things that are happening and things that have happened. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about cause and effect, and hypothetical situations.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "How would you feel if you saw a whale in real life?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"co