kill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "DWS", "template_override": 1}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn9le02ob10re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "Humans have always had a fascination with whales. They have been the subjects of movies and children's stories. Have you heard of the movie <span class=\"italic\">Free Willy</span>? It grossed 157 million dollars worldwide.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn9le02ob10re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "Unfortunately, whales are also the subject of environmentalists' concerns. Whereas whale sightings were once a common event in waters around the world, today certain whales are in jeopardy of becoming extinct. Certain species of whale, like the bowhead whale, have been hunted for their whale oil. Whale oil was obtained by boiling strips of blubber harvested from whales. This, of course, means killing the whale and oftentimes, disposing of its carcass which was of no further use. Fortunately, this practice has been outlawed since the 1980s. If this legislation had been introduced earlier, the bowhead whale would not have become endangered.", "id": 2, "time": "13000", "image": "engenn9le02ob10re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "One way to stop whale killing is to get involved. It might seem a little strange, but it is possible to \"adopt\" a whale and protect the species from extinction. Environmental groups are collecting donations through \"adopt-a-whale\" projects. The money they raise from these \"adoptions\" is being used to rescue whales from fishing nets, help enforce wildlife protection laws, and do research.<br/>\nThe project is also educating people and public awareness is being raised. If people are made more aware of this issue, further research and development of preservation strategies can be achieved.  If you could adopt a whale, would you?", "id": 3, "time": "58000", "image": "engenn9le02ob10re2img03.jpg"}], "audiosrc": "engenn9le02ob10re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn9le02ob10re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "_data": [], "type": "audio", "template_override": 1}]}]}